# Math-First Implementation & LaTeX Alignment

- **Math parity**: Any code change must have matching formulas/derivations in Markdown or LaTeX. Keep symbol names and hyperparameters consistent between equations and code.
- **Novel ideas**: Provide concise derivations (losses, gradients, constraints) and indicate how they map to modules/functions. Prefer explicit objective statements before coding.
- **Documentation targets**: Update the relevant README/notebook section and LaTeX templates when modifying algorithms; keep notation synchronized across text, figures, and code.
- **No silent drift**: If defaults or schedules change, reflect them in the written equations and descriptions.
- **Precision**: Specify variable domains, shapes, and norms in derivations; highlight assumptions (e.g., discount factors, KL weights).
